          %h2#idea Idea
          %p The term ‘rank’ is used in many contexts to number levels within a hierarchy.
          %h2#rank_of_a_module Rank of a module
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/module"} module
            over
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            and we speak of the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            of
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi N
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            = succeed ":" do
              %em rank
          %p
            A collection of elements
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi w
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (w_i)_{i \in I}
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            is called a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/basis"} basis
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            (over
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in N
            there is a unique collection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi i
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a_i)_{i \in I}
            of elements of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi a
                    %mi i
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a_i = 0
            for all but finitely many
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \in I
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mi a
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi w
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x = \sum_{i \in I} a_i w_i
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            has a basis it is called a
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+module"} free module
            (over
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            (the
            = succeed ")," do
              %strong invariant basis number rings
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinality"} cardinality
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo #
                  %mi I
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} # I
            only depends on
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            and not on the choice of basis. It is called the
            %strong rank
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            over
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi rank
                      %mi A
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi M
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} rank_A(M)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            is called the
            = succeed "." do
              %strong
                free module of rank
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo #
                      %mi I
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} # I
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi N
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finitely+generated"} finitely generated
            free module then the rank is a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+number"} finite number
          %p
            All of the following are invariant basis rings (source:
            = succeed "):" do
              %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Invariant_basis_number"} Wikipedia
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                any nontrivial
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi K
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+ring"} group ring
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi G
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K(G)
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi K
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
                any
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
                (or nontrival commutative ring?) and
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi G
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
                any
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group"} group
            %li
              %p
                any
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Noetherian+ring"} Noetherian ring
          %p
            Besides the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trivial+ring"} trivial ring
            (over which any module is free with any set as basis), an example of a ring without invariant basis number is the ring of
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi ℵ
                      %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \aleph_0
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix"} matrices
            (over any ring) in which each column has only finitely many nonzero entries (which allows multiplication to be defined). As a module over itself, this ring is free on any inhabited finite set, as may be shown by using the equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℵ
                    %mn 0
                  %mo =
                  %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi ℵ
                    %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \aleph_0 = n \aleph_0
            (applied to the columns).
          %h2#RankOfALinearMap Rank of a linear map
          %p
            Given a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+map"} linear map
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
            of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/modules"} modules
            = succeed "-module." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/image"} image
          %p
            Often this is considered for the case that the linear map is represented by a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/matrix"} matrix
            and one speaks of the
            = succeed "." do
              %em rank of a matrix
          %h2#rank_of_a_sheaf_of_modules Rank of a sheaf of modules
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo ,
                  %mi 𝒪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (X,\mathcal{O})
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/locally+ringed+space"} locally ringed space
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            a
            = succeed "-module." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝒪
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}
            %em rank
            at a point
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in X
            is the vector space dimension of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≔
                  %msub
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mi x
                  %msub
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi 𝒪
                        %mi x
                  %mi k
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}(x) \coloneqq \mathcal{E}_x \otimes_{\mathcal{O}_x} k(x)
            over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/residue+field"} residue field
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k(x)
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            is of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coherent+sheaf"} finite type
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            can equivalently be defined as the minimal number of elements needed to generate the stalk
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi ℰ
                    %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}_x
            as a
            = succeed "-module" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi 𝒪
                      %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_x
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nakayama%27s+lemma"} Nakayama's lemma
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semicontinuous+map"} upper semicontinuous
            function
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo →
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \mathbb{N}
          %p
            In the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+logic"} internal language
            of the sheaf topos
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Sh
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Sh}(X)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            can internally quite simply be defined as the minimal number of elements needed to generate
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            (taken as an element of the suitably completed natural numbers, i.e. the poset of inhabited upper sets). Under the correspondence of internal inhabited upper sets in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi{:mathvariant => "normal"} Sh
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi X
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathrm{Sh}(X)
            and upper semicontinuous functions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \to \mathbb{N}
            (details at
            = succeed ")," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/one-sided+real+number"} one-sided real number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            is of finite type; see
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "http://mathoverflow.net/questions/34412/the-upper-semi-continuous-rank-of-a-module-sheaf"} this MathOverflow question
          %p
            See also
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank+of+a+coherent+sheaf"} rank of a coherent sheaf
          %h2#rank_of_a_vector_bundle Rank of a vector bundle
          %p
            As a simple special case of the above, a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+bundle"} vector bundle
            is said to have
            %em
              rank
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            if each
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fiber"} fiber
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+space"} vector space
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %h2#hereditary_rank_of_a_pure_set Hereditary rank of a pure set
          %p
            Every
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pure+set"} pure set
            within the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/von+Neumann+hierarchy"} von Neumann hierarchy
            appears first at some level given by an
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinal+number"} ordinal number
            = succeed "." do
              %strong hereditary rank
          %p
            We may define this rank explicitly (and
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/recursion"} recursively
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi rank
                  %mi S
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi S
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi rank
                  %mi x
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} rank S = \bigcup_{x \in S} (rank x)^+ ,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bigcup
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supremum"} supremum
            operation on ordinals (literally the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/union"} union
            for
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/von+Neumann+ordinals"} von Neumann ordinals
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo +
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^+
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/successor"} successor
            operation (which is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ↦
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∪
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi a
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \mapsto a \cup \{a\}
            for von Neumann ordinals).
          %h2#rank_of_a_functor Rank of a functor
          %p
            Recall that a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cardinal+number"} cardinal number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            is said to be
            %em regular
            if
            = succeed "<" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋃
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi I
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |\bigcup_{i\in I} X_i |
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            whenever
            = succeed "<" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |I|
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            and
            = succeed "<" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |X_i|
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi I
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i\in I
          %p
            A functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                  %mo :
                  %mi 𝒜
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℬ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F:\mathcal{A}\to \mathcal{B}
            %em has rank
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            for some regular cardinal
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            preserves
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/filtered+colimit"} filtered colimits
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi F
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F
            %em has rank
            when it has rank
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi α
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            for some regular cardinal
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
            = succeed ")" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi α
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \alpha
          %p
            The properties of functors with rank are discussed in section 5.5 of Borceux (
            %a{:href => "#Borceux2"}> 1994
            ).
          %h2#rank_of_a_lie_group Rank of a Lie group
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank-nullity+theorem"} rank-nullity theorem
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank+of+a+Lie+group"} rank of a Lie group
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank+of+a+coherent+sheaf"}> rank of a coherent sheaf
                ,
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/degree+of+a+coherent+sheaf"} degree of a coherent sheaf
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slope+of+a+coherent+sheaf"} slope of a coherent sheaf
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/stable+coherent+sheaf"}> stable coherent sheaf
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Bridgeland+stability+condition"} Bridgeland stability condition
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rank-nullity+theorem"} rank-nullity theorem
          %h2#references References
          %ul
            %li#Borceux2
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Francis+Borceux"}> Francis Borceux
              ,
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Handbook+of+Categorical+Algebra"} Handbook of Categorical Algebra
                vol. 2
              , Cambridge UP 1994.
